   Since \( y = \frac{1}{|S|} \sum_{x_k \in S} x_k \), we have:
   \[
   x_i - y = x_i - \frac{1}{|S|} \sum_{x_k \in S} x_k.
   \]
   Therefore,
   \[
   \left\langle x_i - y, x_j - y \right\rangle = \left\langle x_i - \frac{1}{|S|} \sum_{x_k \in S} x_k, x_j - \frac{1}{|S|} \sum_{x_k \in S} x_k \right\rangle.
   \]
   Expanding the inner product:
   \[
   \left\langle x_i - \frac{1}{|S|} \sum_{x_k \in S} x_k, x_j - \frac{1}{|S|} \sum_{x_k \in S} x_k \right\rangle = \left\langle x_i, x_j \right\rangle - \frac{1}{|S|} \sum_{x_k \in S} \left\langle x_i, x_k \right\rangle - \frac{1}{|S|} \sum_{x_k \in S} \left\langle x_j, x_k \right\rangle + \frac{1}{|S|^2} \left( \sum_{x_k \in S} \left\langle x_k, x_k \right\rangle \right).
